{{template "layout" .}}
{{define "content" -}}
<p style="margin:0 0 16px;"><strong>Outbound mail works.</strong></p>
<p style="margin:0 0 16px;">
This message was sent by {{.Data.RequestedBy}} from the {{.Product}} admin API to
verify the mail configuration of <a href="{{.BaseURL}}" style="color:#1264a3;">{{.BaseURL}}</a>.
</p>
<table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="margin:0 0 16px;font-size:13px;color:#1d1c1d;">
<tr><td style="padding:2px 12px 2px 0;color:#616061;">Transport</td><td style="padding:2px 0;"><code>{{.Data.Transport}}</code></td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:2px 12px 2px 0;color:#616061;">Sent at</td><td style="padding:2px 0;"><code>{{.Data.SentAt.UTC.Format "2 January 2006 at 15:04:05 UTC"}}</code></td></tr>
</table>
<p style="margin:0;color:#616061;font-size:13px;">
Receiving this message proves the transport accepted it for delivery. It does not
prove anything about deliverability to other domains: SPF, DKIM and DMARC
alignment, plus the sending IP's reputation, decide whether real recipients see
mail in the inbox or in the spam folder.
</p>
{{- end}}
